This study investigates the existence of multiple solutions to an Kirchhoff type elliptic system governed by Trudinger-Moser growth nonlinearity. By employing variational techniques, superlevel analysis, and the variational saddle-saddle theorem, it is demonstrated that three distinct solutions emerge within a small neighborhood of the origin when the Kirchhoff coefficient satisfies appropriate constraints. Furthermore, a fourth solution is identified in cases where the parameter lies within certain intervals; alongside the previously mentioned solutions near the origin, this additional solution is characterized as a mountain pass type.

